1061	1108	Biography
Dubravka Šuica was born in Dubrovnik.
1109	1246	She graduated from the Zagreb Faculty of Humanities and Social Sciences in 1981, majoring in English and literature and German language.

1246	1384	Before her political career, Dubravka Šuica worked for 20 years as a high school teacher, university professor and principal in Dubrovnik.
1385	1513	She became active in politics in 1990, joining Croatian Democratic Union (HDZ) before the first democratic elections in Croatia.
1514	1584	Since 1998, she served as head of HDZ Dubrovnik branch up until 2014.

1584	1651	In 2001, Šuica was elected as first ever female mayor of Dubrovnik.
1652	1714	She was re-elected in 2005 and served as the mayor till 2009.

1714	1831	She was elected as the member of Croatian Parliament three times, in the 2000, 2003 and 2007 parliamentary elections.
1832	1893	She held several positions in Croatian Parliament Committees.
1894	2081	She was Chairwoman of the committee, Family, Youth and Sports (2000–2003) and also vice-chairwoman of the Committee on European Affairs during the Croatia's accession period (2007–2011).

2081	2219	In 2004, Dubravka Šuica was elected one of the vice-presidents of the Congress of Local and Regional Authorities of the Council of Europe.
2220	2285	She was reelected to that position in 2006, 2008, 2010 and 2012.

2285	2373	In May 2012, Dubravka Šuica was elected vice-president of the HDZ at the national level.
2374	2455	She was also the president of the Foreign and European Affairs Committee of HDZ.

2455	2551	In October 2012, she was elected vice-president of EPP Women and she still holds this position.

2551	2643	In the 2013 European election, Dubravka Šuica was elected Member of the European Parliament.
2644	2717	She was sworn in on 1 July 2013, after Croatia joined the European Union.
2718	2807	She was re-elected MEP following the 2014 European election, placing 2nd on the HDZ list.
